WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.570
- So, how did you land
the role on "Ted Lasso",

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.050
other than being perfect for it?

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:04.883
(all laugh)

00:00:04.883 --> 00:00:05.716
- Well, thank you.

00:00:05.716 --> 00:00:09.590
Well, I studied my Master
in Acting in the UK.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.850
I saved money over there
and before going to the UK,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.020
and then I was in Mexico

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.100
and I received the
audition for "Ted Lasso".

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.760
I did it, didn't hear anything.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.890
They started shooting in August,

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.200
So I thought, "Well, nothing happened."

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.760
But then I received a random
tweet from Bill Lawrence,

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.247
a showrunner of the show who said, just,

00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:29.924
"Good audition, man."

00:00:29.924 --> 00:00:31.040
(all laughing)
- [Kelly] Really?

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.820
- And I was like, okay, either
he's playing with my feelings

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.770
or there's something good happening.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.720
- Oh my God that'd be so mean.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.553
So mean.
- Yeah.

00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:42.700
And then I did more
auditions and story short,

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.980
I got the role for an Icelandic man.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.370
So when I arrived on set,

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.207
I was called Gooner, and I was like,

00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:50.630
"If I'm playing an Icelandic man,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.350
I need more preparation."
- Wait, what?

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.690
So originally it wasn't even
the role you're in right now?

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:56.523
- No, no, no.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.670
The role was for a guy from Iceland,

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.734
but they liked my audition,
from what I know now,

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:05.840
that they kept it and that's why

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.909
they adapted it to who I am and I got-

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:09.742
(applause drowns out sound)
- Oh my God,

00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:11.076
I love it, you were so great.

00:01:11.076 --> 00:01:13.176
(guest applaud)
That's amazing (giggles)!

